    Add multi-source network discovery and direct wallet links
    
    network_discovery.mjs — what each named source actually contributes:
      Solscan    API key-gated, so origin tracing runs against Solana RPC
                 directly. Same data, no key. Solscan used for links only.
      Bubblemaps no public API. Its graph is reproducible from chain — wallets
                 sharing a funding origin — so the cluster logic is computed,
                 not fetched.
      GMGN       403 Cloudflare.  Win rate / PnL / trade count CANNOT be
      Birdeye    401 paid key.    fetched. Verified across several attempts.
    
    So discovered wallets carry deep links to GMGN and Birdeye instead of
    fabricated stats, and the alert says so. All three profile URLs 403 to
    curl — that is anti-scraping, not a broken link; they open from a phone.
    
    Expansion safety, because auto-enrolling wallets is self-destructive:
      - HIGH-DEGREE FUNDERS REJECTED. One CEX hot wallet funds thousands of
        unrelated users; without this the net would enrol half of Solana in a
        day and every token would "match smart money". Verified: 40 wallets
        behind one funder yields 0 clusters and a logged rejection.
      - Expansion only proceeds from a cluster already containing a tracked
        wallet, so the net grows along evidence.
      - Caps per run and total, with provenance recorded per entry.
    
    Discoveries write to discovered_wallets.json, NOT smart_wallets.json —
    auto_top_whales.mjs rewrites the latter wholesale every 2h and would have
    silently erased them. loadWatchlist now merges both, curated entries
    winning on duplicate addresses.
    
    Part 2 needed no change: the 20% cap, 150-holder floor, mint/freeze/LP
    gates and score-0 override were already in force and verified.
    
    Caught while wiring: two console calls landed empty via shell escaping.
    Valid JS, so --check passed — a silent failure only visible by reading
    the emitted code.
    
