    Add automated sell-signal notifier with three exit triggers
    
    Positions open when a BUY alert is delivered, capturing the market cap at
    that moment and each insider's token balance. Taken any later the baseline
    would already include selling, so the capture happens inline with the
    alert.
    
    Triggers, each firing at most once per position:
      1 INSIDER EXIT  insider balance down >=40% from baseline (one RPC call
                      per wallet; verified 202ms, and a probe wallet was
                      already at zero)
      2 TAKE PROFIT   market cap reached 2x entry
      3 STOP LOSS     market cap 20% below entry, OR the pair delisted
    
    Deliberate choices:
      - Once-only firing, or a token sitting at -21% would re-send a stop-loss
        every 30 seconds.
      - TAKE_PROFIT does NOT close the position: its advice is to remove
        initial capital and let the rest run, so the stop-loss must stay armed
        on the remainder. STOP_LOSS and INSIDER_EXIT do close it.
      - A delisted pair is a stop-loss, not missing data. Liquidity being
        pulled is the most important thing to be told about, and silence would
        be the worst response.
      - Percentages are stated as movement from the ALERT market cap, never as
        P&L. Aegis does not know the user's fill, size, or whether they took
        the trade — claiming otherwise would invent a fact about their money.
    
    Monitor runs every scan and every loop tick, not on the maintenance
    cadence: an insider exit or a rug is time-critical.
    
    Verified across 9 trigger cases including boundaries (-19% vs -25%,
    sold 30% vs 55%) and re-fire suppression.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

